    bare_name_registry_collision_trigger_conditions_2026-07-30, 1, "2026-11-10 status fixing->open: stale sweep claim, no lane active; reopened for P2 burn-down"
    bare_name_registry_collision_trigger_conditions_2026-07-30, 2, "2026-11-10 lane-p2-barename (Fable): TRIGGER CONDITIONS ESTABLISHED and pinned. named_type_register (types.spl) is a flat bare-name pool that is reset per module on the flat-AST bridge path (module_assembly.spl reset_all_pools before every parser_init_with_path) but NOT on the append-mode parse path parse_module_file (core interpreter module_loader_core.spl:342 / module_loader_lazy.spl:568, legacy C driver). There, a second module declaring the same bare struct name got the FIRST module id back and named_type_update clobbered that module field layout (red: expected 0 to not equal 0; first-module fields became the second-module fields). The small-program probes in the .md could never see this because they ran on the seed or on the per-module-reset HIR path. FIX: registry entries record their declaring module (named_type_modules, set by parser_init_with_path/parse_module_file via named_type_set_current_module); named_type_register never adopts another module declared (non-empty-layout) entry and allocates a fresh id instead, while an empty-layout placeholder (forward reference) is still adopted and claimed; named_type_find prefers the current module own declaration, then the first registration (pre-fix behaviour for imports). Spec test/01_unit/compiler/frontend/named_type_registry_cross_module_collision_spec.spl 3 examples: red 0/1 (clobber probe) -> green 3/3. Siblings green: flat_type_pool_scope_owner, local_generic_annotation, option_generic_inner_type_gaps, private_glob_import_module_local_resolution (PR #8208). Pre-existing unrelated reds on base and branch alike: compiler_core/types_spec (1/5), sized_array_type_retention (0/12), type_subst_if_chain_source (missing export if_chain_nodes). Remaining gap, not closed: a bare-name reference from a THIRD module that imports one of two same-named declarations still resolves to the first registration (the registry has no import visibility); HIR resolves by its own scoped symbol table so this affects only the parse-time tag."

